From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:24:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): switch a running session's account from the
 harness menu

Carried on custom while the design is discussed on upstream issue #503;
see docs/providers.md. Drop it once upstream has an equivalent.

The server can now move a running Claude session to another provider, but
the composer had no way to ask for it, and it did not show which account a
session runs on.

The in-session harness menu gains the same Account section as the
new-session dialog, for host-bound claude-native and claude-sdk sessions
whose host lists more than one provider. The current account is checked.
Accounts that are not signed in, or that keep a separate login and
conversation store (a different switch group), are listed but disabled with
the reason. Picking one calls POST /v1/sessions/{id}/provider and says
whether Claude is restarting now or switches after the current turn; errors
show the server's message.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Docs: none (documented with its series in docs/providers.md)
